--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,7 +9,10 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 `createRentalService()` (from `src/index.ts`) returns an in-memory service with `addEquipment`, `quote`,
 `book` and `availability`. Money is integer euro cents; a rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price (rounded to the nearest cent), in both quotes and bookings; times are ISO-8601 UTC strings. A period starts and ends at
 midnight UTC and `end` is the start of the day after the last rented day, so `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z` to
-`2026-07-03T00:00:00Z` is two days. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods. `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the sorted ids of the equipment of that kind (any kind if
+`2026-07-03T00:00:00Z` is two days. An item added with an `hourlyPrice` (cents per hour) can also be rented by the
+hour: a period shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour (e.g. `2026-07-01T14:00:00Z` to
+`2026-07-01T17:00:00Z`) costs the hourly price for each hour, with no long-stay discount. Items without an
+`hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour, and `availability` for such a period lists only items that have one. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods. `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the sorted ids of the equipment of that kind (any kind if
 omitted) with no booking overlapping the period; it throws on an invalid period or kind. Cancellation
 (no refund under 24 hours before the start, otherwise full refund) is not implemented yet.
 
